  "_methodology": [
    "Ground truth for sluggify(name) === slug pairs, extracted from the real Foundry pf2e-8.3.0 pack snapshot (apps/codex/data/snapshots/foundry/pf2e-8.3.0/packs/pf2e/).",
    "The snapshot has NO system.slug field anywhere (verified exhaustively: 0/28,636 docs carry a system.slug key, of any value, at the document top level) -- so \"pack docs already carry system.slug\" does not hold for this snapshot literally.",
    "Ground truth is instead the PACK FILE'S OWN BASENAME: upstream's own extraction tooling (foundryvtt/pf2e's pack build step) names every source JSON file after the document's slug. This was verified exhaustively, not sampled: an exhaustive scan of all 28,636 docs found filename === sluggify(name) for EVERY SINGLE ONE (0 disagreements, 0% disagreement rate) -- see the codex-0029 gotchas memory entry for the full script. No pair required exclusion.",
    "This file is a small, hand-curated, DETERMINISTIC subset of that exhaustive check: ~90 evenly-strided samples across the whole corpus (sorted file order, every Nth file) plus every tricky-character example the extraction script found (apostrophes, diacritics, parenthesized qualifiers, dashes, ampersands, ellipses, non-breaking hyphens, curly quotes, embedded nicknames, colons, slashes, commas, leading plus signs) -- committed so CI can assert the port without touching the gitignored data/ directory."
